         if(updateObject)
         {
-            if(this._mannequinScale !== scale)
-            {
-                this._mannequinScale = scale;
-
-                this.updateAvatar();
-            }
+            if(this._mannequinScale !== scale) this._mannequinScale = scale;
+
+            // pixelrp: a mannequin would not turn.
+            //
+            // The direction changes here as well as the scale, and the avatar
+            // image is baked per direction - getAvatarAssetName() carries the
+            // direction in its name. Stock only regenerated it when the SCALE
+            // changed, so after a rotate the asset for the new direction had
+            // never been made, avatarExists() was false, and getSpriteAssetName
+            // fell back to the bundle's static layer art.
+            //
+            // For boutique_mannequin1 that art is the same pixels eight times
+            // over: every _64_a_<dir>_0 and _64_b_<dir>_0 is an alias of the
+            // direction-0 asset, at identical offsets, with no flip. So the
+            // piece rotated on the server, bounced on screen, and drew exactly
+            // what it drew before. The figure is the only part that can turn,
+            // and nothing was asking it to.
+            //
+            // updateAvatar() no-ops when the asset for the current direction
+            // already exists, so this costs a lookup on an ordinary update.
+            if(this._figure) this.updateAvatar();
         }
 
         return updateObject;
